Analysis stage: panels -> matching -> figures -> tables/text -> R regressions.
Run with `python run.py --stage analysis` (or `python analysis/main.py`) from anywhere; every
script can also be run on its own from the repository root. Inputs: preprocessing/data/03_output.

  python analysis/src/d00_preprocessing/gathering.py   -> data/{daily,intraday}_{main,balanced}.parquet
      main = firms with >= 1 trading day before and after 24 Feb 2022 (all their days kept);
      balanced = firms on every trading day of the union calendar (robustness). Rows need quoted and
      effective spread, trades, dollar volume, market value, price impact and realized spread.
  python analysis/src/d00_preprocessing/matching.py    -> data/psm_assignments.parquet (matched_group, eb_weight), data/psm_balance.csv
      one matching on pre-period firm medians of log market value, log dollar volume (USD) and log
      quoted spread: Mahalanobis distance within an adaptive propensity caliper, 1:1 without
      replacement (optimal assignment); entropy-balancing weights as robustness.
  python analysis/src/d01_figures/daily.py             -> output/figures/daily/{main,balanced}/{full,matched,eb}/
  python analysis/src/d01_figures/intraday.py          -> output/figures|tables/intraday/... (open/close-hour z-scores, Welch t-tests)
  python analysis/src/d01_figures/intraday_overnight.py-> output/figures|tables/overnight/...
  python analysis/src/d01_figures/descriptives.py      -> output/figures|tables/map/... (+ firms_by_country.tex, longtable)
  python analysis/src/d03_docs/build_sampling_docs.py  -> output/tables/{sample_selection,currencies,matching/balance}.tex,
                                                          ../docs/paper/sampling/{data_section,formulas_appendix}.tex (from the templates)
  Rscript analysis/src/d02_results/run_all.R           -> output/tables/regressions/{matched,main}/ (paper) and internal/{balanced,eb}/
      common.R        root, panels, units (spreads/impact/realized in %, activity in logs of USD, volatility in %),
                      samples, did() = feols with firm + day fixed effects and SEs clustered by firm and day
      descriptives.R  summary statistics, Nearby vs Distant means with clustered differences and DiD, firms by industry
      pretrends.R     treatment x trend on the pre-period, also by distance bin
      baseline.R      neighbour dummies, negative distance (linear TWFE), war-day return, intensity, volatility as outcome
      dose_response.R ATT by distance bin vs firms beyond 3,000 km, ACRT per 1,000 km and dose-weighted
                      average (Callaway, Goodman-Bacon and Sant'Anna 2025), figure, contdid B-spline estimates
      horserace.R     geographic treatment together with the war-day return and pre-war volatility
      mechanism.R     effective = realized spread + price impact; mediation with Gelbach share; pre-war price impact terciles
      intraday.R      Nearby - Distant abnormal opening/closing-hour spreads by day, clustered regression
  Figures carry no titles (the folder says sample and group). Long tables use longtable.

R: system R >= 4.4; `Rscript analysis/R/requirements.R` installs arrow, data.table, fixest (>= 0.14), contdid, ggplot2.
Python: conda env from ../environment.yml. Sample-selection funnel: output/sampling/sampling_log.csv.
